--TEST--
an attribute's name resolves to an attribute declaration and the payload is checked against its fields, so a name nothing declares and a payload that does not fit are refused where they are written — `rule:attributes/an-attribute-is-declared-with-its-sites`, `rule:attributes/attach-sites-and-forms`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:attributes/an-attribute-is-declared-with-the-places-it-may-be-used
// The payload is checked against the declaration's fields by `rule:types/shape-type`'s
// ordinary width subtyping, and not by a second rule of its own. A name that is
// a class, an enum or a `type` alias is pinned by
// `only-an-attribute-declaration-follows-the-attribute-bracket.nvst`.
repeatable attribute Route on class { path: string, method: string }
attribute Tagged on class, property {}

// The accepted half first, so a position that stops being accepted fails here
// rather than as a missing refusal. An extra field is width subtyping and is
// fine, and a use written with no list attaches an empty literal, which
// satisfies a declaration with no field.
#[Route(path: "/users", method: "GET")]
#[Route(path: "/users/:id", method: "GET", version: 2)]
#[Tagged]
class Accepted {
    #[Tagged(extra: true)]
    public string $name = "n";
}

// A name nothing declares is the ordinary `E0303` any unresolvable name is.
#[Undeclared(path: "/x")]
class RefusedName {
    public string $field = "f";
}

// Where the name is a declaration, the literal is checked against it: a field
// of the wrong type, and a field the declaration lists that the payload never
// wrote, are the two halves of that check.
#[Route(path: 3, method: "GET")]
class WrongFieldType {}

#[Route(path: "/x")]
class MissingField {}

echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0303]: `Undeclared` is not declared
   --> case.nvs:23:3
%A
error[E0401]: expected `{ method: string, path: string }`, found `{ method: string, path: int }`
   --> case.nvs:31:8
%A
error[E0401]: expected `{ method: string, path: string }`, found `{ path: string }`
   --> case.nvs:34:8
%A
error: aborting due to 3 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
